-- title:
--   Integrability of the translated split dual finite cell integrand
-- statement:
--   Fix a number field $K$ with an integral algebra structure on $\mathcal O_K$ over $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ and $[K:\mathbb Q]=3$, a Hecke eigensystem $\Phi$ over $\mathbb Q$ with complex coefficients (a nonzero level ideal together with families $\Phi.a,\Phi.b$ indexed by finite places), and a finite set $S_Q$ of finite places of $\mathbb Q$ containing every place dividing the level and such that every prime of $K$ above a place outside $S_Q$ has ramification index $1$; assume $\|\Phi.b_p\|=1$ off $S_Q$ and $\sum_p\|\Phi.a_p\|N(p)^{-\sigma}<\infty$ for $\sigma>1$; let $S_K$ be the set of primes of $K$ above $S_Q$ and $S\subseteq S_Q$. The automorphic input consists of a continuous smooth cuspidal realisation $R$ of $\Phi.\mathrm{toRawCentral}$ (the eigensystem with $b_v$ rescaled by $N(v)^{-1}$) for the pins $\mathrm{productionPinsGeneral}\ \mathbb Q$, with exceptional set inside $S$; an auxiliary function $C_{\mathrm{fin}}$; and a family $\varphi_{\mathrm{par}}$, indexed by parities $\mathrm{InfinitePlace}\ \mathbb Q\to\mathbb Z/2$, of nonzero isotypic cusp forms at those pins with central character $R.\mathrm{centralChar}$, level $\Phi.\mathrm{level}$ and exceptional set $S$ for $\Phi$, each fixed by right convolution against some factorisable test function. Further data: an admissible twist $\mu$ of the ideles of $K$ (idele class, continuous, unitary); a global additive character $\psi$ with all local levels $0$ and $\psi^{-1}=\psi_{\mathbb Q}$; a cubic induction form $F$ for $(K,\psi,\mu)$ over the pins built from the class-representative Siegel set $\mathrm{classRepSiegelSet}\ \mathbb Q\ (1/2)\ 1\ (1/2)\ 2$, the levels $\mathrm{levelOne}\sqcap\mathrm{finiteAdelicGL2Subgroup}$, the Hecke generators and the adelic box, with $F.\mathrm{form}\neq 0$, with $F.\mathrm{whittakerLoc}_v(1)=1$ and spherical torus values for $\mathrm{inducedCoeff}\ K\ \mu$ at places unramified in $K$ whose local additive level is $0$, with continuous form, Whittaker and dual Whittaker functions, the latter two gauge majorised, and with the bad-place hypothesis that on every finite set $T$ each local Whittaker function at a bad place of $T$ is right invariant under an open subgroup and lies in the cyclic subspace generated by each of its nonzero cyclic subspaces. Finally: a finite set $S'\supseteq S_Q$ outside which no place is bad; uniformisers $\varpi_p$ at the places off $S_Q$ (nonzero with valuation $\exp(-1)$); the finite central translate $h_\mu$ in $\mathrm{finiteAdelicGL2Subgroup}\ \mathbb Q$ given as the product over $p\in S'\setminus S_Q$ of the place embeddings of the scalar matrices $\varpi_p^{-\mathrm{inducedLevelAt}\ K\ \mu\ p}$; a splitting $W_A,W_f$ of the $\psi_{\mathbb Q}$-Whittaker coefficient of $\varphi_{\mathrm{par}}$ at $1$ as $W_A(\mathrm{ratArchGL2}\ g)\cdot W_f(\mathrm{finFactor}\ g)$, with $W_f=C_{\mathrm{fin}}(1,\cdot)$ and $W_f(1)\neq 0$; the element $w_0\in\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb Q)$ with matrix $\begin{pmatrix}0&1\\1&0\end{pmatrix}$ and the dual finite factor $W_f^\vee(g_f)=\|\det g_f\|\,W_f(\mathrm{finFactor}(w_0\cdot{}^t g_f^{-1}))$; Haar measures $\mu_f$ on the finite adelic $\mathrm{GL}_2$ and $\mu_{N}$ on its finite unipotent subgroup; and a parity $\mathrm{par}$ for which $W_f^\vee$ is measurable and satisfies $W_f^\vee(ng)=\theta(n)W_f^\vee(g)$ with $|\theta(n)|=1$ for every finite unipotent $n$; together with elements $kk_p\in\mathrm{GL}_3(\mathbb Q_p)$ for $p\in S_Q$. The conclusion asserts the existence of $\sigma\in\mathbb R$ such that for every $s'$ with $\mathrm{Re}\,s'>\sigma$ and every $\hat z$ in the finite adelic $\mathrm{GL}_2$ whose local component is $1$ at each place off $S_Q$, the function $$g\mapsto \mathbf 1_{\mathcal C}(g\hat z)\,W_f^\vee(g\hat z\,h_\mu)\prod_{p\in S_Q}F.\mathrm{whittakerLoc}_p\bigl(w_3\,{}^t\iota(\,(g\hat z)_p)^{-1}kk_p\bigr)\cdot\mathbf 1_{\mathcal C}(g\hat z)\prod_{v\notin S_Q}^{\mathrm{f}}\mathrm{dualWhittakerFn3}\,(F.\mathrm{whittakerLoc}_v)\bigl(\iota((g\hat z\,h_\mu)_v)\bigr)\cdot\|\det (g\hat z)\|^{\,s'-1/2}$$ is integrable against $\mu_f$ weighted by the density $\mathrm{HaarQuotient.density}$ of the finite unipotent subgroup for $\mu_N$; here $\mathcal C$ is the set of $g$ whose component at each place $p\notin S_Q$ lies in the product of the image of $\mathrm{unipotentGL2Hom}$ and $\mathrm{AdelicDock.localLevelOne}\ p\ \top$, $w_3=\mathrm{longWeyl3}$, $\iota=\mathrm{iotaGL}$ is the embedding $\mathrm{GL}_2\hookrightarrow\mathrm{GL}_3$, $\mathrm{dualWhittakerFn3}\,W(g)=W(w_3\,{}^tg^{-1})$, the product over $v\notin S_Q$ is a finprod with the factors at $v\in S_Q$ set to $1$, and $\|\cdot\|$ is $\mathrm{ideleNorm}\ \mathbb Q$.
--
--   This is an absolute-convergence statement for the finite part of a $\mathrm{GL}_3\times\mathrm{GL}_2$ Rankin–Selberg integral in its split, dual form: the $\hat z$-translate of the cell integrand, built from the dual finite Whittaker factor of the $\mathrm{GL}_2$ eigenform, the local $\mathrm{GL}_3$ Whittaker functions at the places of $S_Q$ and the dual spherical factors away from $S_Q$, is integrable on a right half-plane in $s'$. It feeds the isolation of the remainder terms in the finite-family assembly of the Langlands–Tunnell converse theorem, being used by [`LanglandsTunnell.RankinSelberg.exists_forall_integrable_cutoff_remainder_mul_finprod_away`](thm.html#LanglandsTunnell.RankinSelberg.exists_forall_integrable_cutoff_remainder_mul_finprod_away).
